1
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:35,100
you

2
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
so

3
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:56,230
much

4
00:00:56,313 --> 00:00:57,143
for watching.

5
00:01:33,473 --> 00:01:34,303
oh, oh, oh,

6
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:54,720
Cruel fate.

7
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,080
Kuma's decision as a father.

8
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:05,077
I'm here on business, I'm afraid.

9
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:07,080
It's awfully cold here.

10
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:09,660
Nothing like Punk Hazard at all.

11
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:16,277
Climate aside, this is where the future
of mankind itself will be created.

12
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:21,640
Honestly, dealing with the constant flow
of ideas is my biggest issue right now!

13
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:24,020
I can tell.

14
00:02:24,900 --> 00:02:29,253
You've been too distracted to notice
some of the finer points of this lab.

15
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:46,857
I see what is the issue
not a word gets past us,

16
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:49,797
especially not any secret
deals with pirates.

17
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,380
Oh Stop it.

18
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:53,400
Don't you dare stop Borsalino.

19
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:55,974
You know I can't stand this side of you

20
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:58,240
It's not personal friend.

21
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,860
I told you this is business

22
00:03:08,740 --> 00:03:10,377
Is this Porcelino?

23
00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:11,290
Yes, sir.

24
00:03:11,373 --> 00:03:12,397
I'm in the lab now.

25
00:03:12,480 --> 00:03:15,277
And you, Vega? Punk?

26
00:03:15,360 --> 00:03:16,357
Are you listening?

27
00:03:16,440 --> 00:03:18,297
I am.

28
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,777
Doctor.

29
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:24,037
I know our priorities are
different, but have some sense.

30
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,997
Kuma is strong. Of course.

31
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:29,021
He would make a fine base
for your clone soldiers.

32
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:33,140
But he is a pirate
wanted for $296 million.

33
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:37,860
A man like that cannot serve
as a symbol of justice.

34
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:40,380
Think of the Navy's reputation.

35
00:03:40,860 --> 00:03:42,820
I don't care about saving face.

36
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,540
If the project succeeds, we'll be
saving lives, far more important.

37
00:03:48,240 --> 00:03:49,100
That's true.

38
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:52,177
We can hardly ignore the
potential of such an endeavor,

39
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:54,672
assuming that you can see it to fruition.

40
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:58,540
And yet, I have terms.

41
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:01,620
Bartholomew Kuma,

42
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:07,100
if you're listening, my first demand is
that you join the seven warlords of the sea.

43
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,070
Recently,

44
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:14,142
a rookie named Ace took one of them down,
and we've been looking for a replacement.

45
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,840
The pirate world is in a state of chaos.

46
00:04:18,560 --> 00:04:21,960
We need a man of your
caliber to rein it in.

47
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:23,670
Second,

48
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:28,980
in addition to the clones, you yourself
must become a human weapon for the Navy.

49
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:33,680
Are you saying I'd become a cyborg?

50
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:35,060
That's correct.

51
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:40,220
Then as a warlord, you could triumph
against any pirate in the world.

52
00:04:40,480 --> 00:04:42,009
That'd make me safer, too.

53
00:04:42,100 --> 00:04:43,277
You want that, don't you, friend?

54
00:04:43,360 --> 00:04:44,720
Shut up, Kizaru!

55
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,260
I'm not finished.

56
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:50,717
Kuma, you also have history
with the Revolutionary Army.

57
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:56,020
Needless to say, that is a clear
conflict of interest for the government.

58
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:00,720
Which brings me to my third condition.

59
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:07,140
When the process ends, your mind
and free will will be erased.

60
00:05:08,540 --> 00:05:09,620
I'm sad!

61
00:05:09,900 --> 00:05:12,665
That is nothing but a
glorified death sentence!

62
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:15,417
Is this because the other
warlords won't obey?

63
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:18,980
A cyborg without free will
is a soulless robot! What?

64
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,240
You turn me into a murderer?

65
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:23,180
Is that what you want?

66
00:05:23,620 --> 00:05:26,940
You are in no position to argue with me.

67
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:29,460
You are a Navy scientist.

68
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:34,820
Those are the conditions for saving
the life of a criminal's daughter.

69
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:37,360
If you do not accept,

70
00:05:37,620 --> 00:05:43,020
then we will not spend a fortune on
surgeries to save some insignificant girl.

71
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:55,140
Hey, no running in the lab, please.

72
00:05:57,860 --> 00:06:00,500
This is wrong. It's murder.

73
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,820
Performing such an
operation would be inhumane.

74
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:07,670
Vagabunk.

75
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:13,600
I want you to do it, Kuma.

76
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:19,081
I thought he was going to
make impossible demands.

77
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:22,057
I thought that I wouldn't
be able to save my daughter,

78
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:24,022
but I have nothing more to fear.

79
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:28,900
Thank you.

80
00:06:29,380 --> 00:06:34,580
If you can help Bonnie get well,
then I'll happily accept any fate.

81
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:37,070
Kuma.

82
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,220
Sentomaru, about the matter we discussed.

83
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:47,910
Huh?

84
00:06:49,700 --> 00:06:53,380
One, two, one, two, three.

85
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:55,290
Huh?

86
00:06:56,020 --> 00:06:58,360
Little brat, come back!

87
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:06,500
Vegapunk, how long until Kuma is modified
and his daughter's treatment is complete?

88
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,677
The sapphire scale surgeries
will take six months and then

89
00:07:10,760 --> 00:07:14,231
she'll have to wait another
year before she can go outside.

90
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:17,220
Kuma's modifications
should take two years.

91
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:18,460
I'm so happy.

92
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:21,974
This means body will be better
before her 10th birthday.

93
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:24,740
Your daughter will be our hostage.

94
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:29,480
Once she recovers, you will
have no reason to obey us.

95
00:07:29,660 --> 00:07:31,217
You could take her and run.

96
00:07:31,300 --> 00:07:32,720
I won't run, I swear!

97
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:35,000
We can't be too safe.

98
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:38,697
When her surgeries are complete,
we'll take custody of her.

99
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:43,397
As soon as your free will is gone,
then she will be allowed to leave.

100
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:46,677
And Kuma won't be able to see
her after she gets married!

101
00:07:46,760 --> 00:07:47,817
That is correct.

102
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:49,537
Here is what will happen.

103
00:07:49,620 --> 00:07:54,837
You'll perform Kuma's surgeries while
he serves as one of the seven warlords.

104
00:07:54,920 --> 00:08:00,517
Once his daughter is cured, he will
be forbidden to contact her or escape.

105
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:05,500
If that rule is violated, she'll
be sent off to become a slave?

106
00:08:06,500 --> 00:08:07,937
I'll never visit her.

107
00:08:08,020 --> 00:08:09,860
But I have just one request.

108
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:12,537
I don't want her to know the truth about

109
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:15,267
her disease or the fact
that she's a hostage.

110
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:20,177
So after her surgeries don't make
her stay at some government facility.

111
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:22,457
I Want you to let her
rest at the church in the

112
00:08:22,540 --> 00:08:27,277
sorbet kingdom where she grew up
Nothing more, but right. I promise.

113
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,937
I'll never go there to see her.

114
00:08:29,020 --> 00:08:31,000
I'll do exactly as you command

115
00:08:35,980 --> 00:08:36,820
Very well

116
00:08:38,020 --> 00:08:40,720
It doesn't matter where she's under watch.

117
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:43,920
These next two years will be interesting.

118
00:08:45,600 --> 00:08:46,430
Calick.

119
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:55,300
Hey, Dad!

120
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,230
Huh?

121
00:08:57,313 --> 00:08:58,143
Bonnie!

122
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:01,320
Were you bored?

123
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,920
Sorry about that.

124
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:05,480
Hope you were a good girl. Always!

125
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,510
Uncle!

126
00:09:16,320 --> 00:09:17,150
Huh?

127
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:21,580
Bonnie, we're staying here for
the next six months. We are?

128
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:24,260
Then you'll be here with me? Yep.

129
00:09:24,620 --> 00:09:27,077
Turns out you're not the
only one who needs treatment.

130
00:09:27,160 --> 00:09:27,990
I do, too.

131
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:29,677
Then we'll get better together!

132
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,590
Yay!

133
00:09:32,660 --> 00:09:34,960
Dad, this weird guy is Saint Bonnie.

134
00:09:35,160 --> 00:09:36,217
Wow, so polite.

135
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,418
I know she can be quite the handful.

136
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,759
Please be patient.

137
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,960
Yeah, fine. I'm grateful.

138
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,400
Hey, guess what?

139
00:09:47,720 --> 00:09:51,367
This place is like a big maze
and it doesn't have any windows.

140
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,577
Wait, were you running around on your own?

141
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:54,940
It's dangerous here.

142
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:56,240
It's fine.

143
00:09:56,460 --> 00:09:58,160
We're just a chicken. Stop!

144
00:09:58,600 --> 00:09:59,541
Don't sneak off!

145
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,840
I have dreams to fulfill!

146
00:10:05,760 --> 00:10:07,537
My hands can't keep up.

147
00:10:07,620 --> 00:10:09,477
Someone must chronicle these endless!

148
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,577
Ideas for me?

149
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:13,317
Eat for me, go to the bathroom for me.

150
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,037
Oh, the violence!

151
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,417
It seizes me.

152
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,717
Can someone help me?

153
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:20,620
Even a cat would do.

154
00:10:23,300 --> 00:10:26,480
If only there were five more of me?

155
00:10:53,940 --> 00:10:55,020
Hey, Bonnie.

156
00:10:56,020 --> 00:10:56,850
Sentomaru.

157
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,360
You holding up?

158
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:01,280
You busy? Let's play!

159
00:11:01,600 --> 00:11:02,430
Come with me!

160
00:11:02,513 --> 00:11:04,617
I have a job to do.

161
00:11:04,700 --> 00:11:09,800
I know you're bored, but I don't have
time to hang out with you every day!

162
00:11:16,520 --> 00:11:18,557
Well, maybe for a little while.

163
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:21,320
Slow down.

164
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,060
Oh, hey, Dad!

165
00:11:52,500 --> 00:11:53,500
Hi there, Bonnie.

166
00:11:54,340 --> 00:11:56,380
What kind of father are you?

167
00:11:57,240 --> 00:11:59,740
Your daughter has no sense of modesty!

168
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:01,117
Isn't this fun?

169
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,840
We're playing horsey!

170
00:12:03,480 --> 00:12:05,200
Your horse looks so friendly.

171
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:11,000
I mean, maybe you should let him
go back to the stable. Okie Dock.

172
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:13,800
I don't think she gets it.

173
00:12:17,020 --> 00:12:17,850
Dad!

174
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:19,350
Huh?

175
00:12:19,433 --> 00:12:20,263
What is it?

176
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:24,200
Wait, why do you have marks all over you?

177
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:26,780
Daddy!

178
00:12:27,700 --> 00:12:29,000
Look, it's you!

179
00:12:31,540 --> 00:12:34,860
It's perfect I'll treasure
this for the rest of my life

180
00:13:05,820 --> 00:13:06,879
Thank you, Bonnie.

181
00:13:07,020 --> 00:13:08,373
We'll see you tomorrow.

182
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,310
Okay.

183
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:15,720
I'm getting so hungry.

184
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:20,560
Is that...

185
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,270
Bonnie!

186
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,357
Hey, I was just about to come get you.

187
00:13:27,440 --> 00:13:28,322
Perfect timing.

188
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:30,211
Are you ready for dinner?

189
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:41,050
AHHHHH!

190
00:13:41,133 --> 00:13:42,140
We're all in!

191
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:46,250
AHHHHH!

192
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:47,430
AHHHHH!

193
00:13:47,513 --> 00:13:48,343
Cheers!

194
00:13:48,426 --> 00:13:50,980
Hey Dad, let's do the thing! Okay.

195
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:52,860
Doom da da da!

196
00:13:53,820 --> 00:13:55,140
Doom da da da!

197
00:13:56,900 --> 00:13:58,640
It's the Nita dance!

198
00:13:58,940 --> 00:14:00,020
Come on, try it!

199
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:02,030
Ha-ha-ha!

200
00:14:02,113 --> 00:14:02,960
Looks like fun!

201
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:05,280
How's this? That's it!

202
00:14:06,120 --> 00:14:08,660
I don't have the Sanofia for this!

203
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,373
Someone's a wallflower.

204
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:12,610
Uncle?

205
00:14:15,760 --> 00:14:16,590
Fine.

206
00:14:16,673 --> 00:14:17,880
I'll try it.

207
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:46,580
All right, you're looking great.

208
00:14:46,900 --> 00:14:49,606
One more year and you'll
be in perfect health.

209
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:53,060
Thank you for everything.

210
00:14:53,900 --> 00:14:54,730
Thanks.

211
00:14:56,680 --> 00:15:00,780
Um, once I get better,
can I come visit you?

212
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,000
Of course you can.

213
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,460
Hey, Dad.

214
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:13,140
Is the sea pretty?

215
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:14,530
Yes.

216
00:15:14,660 --> 00:15:15,660
It's beautiful.

217
00:15:16,440 --> 00:15:18,820
It's no fair. Don't worry.

218
00:15:19,060 --> 00:15:21,236
You'll be able to see it soon enough.

219
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:24,620
You and me together.

220
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:26,090
Yeah.

221
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:27,440
I can't wait.

222
00:15:31,200 --> 00:15:32,030
Bonnie!

223
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:33,250
Kashi!

224
00:15:33,540 --> 00:15:34,800
Welcome home!

225
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:37,160
It's been ages!

226
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:40,180
Are you going to live here again? Uh-huh!

227
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:43,400
My disease will be all gone in a year!

228
00:15:43,520 --> 00:15:45,285
Then I can finally go outside!

229
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:46,480
My goodness!

230
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:47,840
That's wonderful!

231
00:15:48,320 --> 00:15:52,077
You were sad you'd get better before you
were ten and it seems you were right!

232
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:54,780
Is someone in need of a babysitter again?

233
00:15:55,500 --> 00:15:56,880
All bad Connie!

234
00:15:59,900 --> 00:16:02,857
We'd be happy to take care
of Akuma, don't worry.

235
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:04,577
Leave everything to us.

236
00:16:04,660 --> 00:16:07,040
I'm grateful, you've all been too kind.

237
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:12,311
I'm a pirate now, so if I stick around,
it might cause trouble for everyone.

238
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:16,060
It'll likely be over a year
until I can come back? Really?

239
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:20,160
That's so long How about
I write you letters?

240
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,837
When I pick you up, we'll take to the sea.

241
00:16:23,920 --> 00:16:26,177
From there, it's an endless horizon!

242
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:27,820
Yeah, I can't wait.

243
00:16:28,100 --> 00:16:31,000
I want to go all kinds
of places. That's great.

244
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:33,515
I'll take you anywhere you want to go.

245
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:36,460
If only that were true.

246
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:39,600
Don't worry.

247
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,540
She's in good hands.

248
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:43,080
Who is this woman?

249
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:44,897
Per the doctor's orders,

250
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:48,977
I'll be staying with Bonnie until her
treatment's done and she's all better.

251
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:50,937
Every day I'll check her temperature,

252
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,937
give her medicine, and
monitor everything about her.

253
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:55,320
Nothing gets past me.

254
00:16:56,460 --> 00:16:57,560
Hi, Bonnie!

255
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:58,980
I'm Nurse Alpha.

256
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:05,790
Hey!

257
00:17:05,873 --> 00:17:07,557
What's that in front of the church?

258
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,557
That's where Bonnie will be staying.

259
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:13,020
But this hospital doesn't
allow any suspicious visitors,

260
00:17:13,220 --> 00:17:15,514
so make sure you always carry your IDs.

261
00:17:15,800 --> 00:17:17,035
That sounds annoying!

262
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:22,540
One toe out of line.

263
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:30,120
And I'll snap her little neck
I know I won't come back.

264
00:17:34,160 --> 00:17:34,990
Oh.

265
00:17:37,940 --> 00:17:43,440
Goodbye Bonnie and thank you
thank you for being born.

266
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:00,460
Okay, I'm heading out.

267
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,360
Stay safe, okay?

268
00:18:30,700 --> 00:18:33,960
and thus the tyrant became a warlord.

269
00:18:34,580 --> 00:18:38,197
bartholomew kuma was obedient to his
orders from the world government.

270
00:18:38,280 --> 00:18:42,537
it made him a force to be reckoned
with for pirates across the world.

271
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:45,580
young master it says here
there's a new warlord?

272
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,700
Kuma the Tyrant, huh?

273
00:18:51,280 --> 00:18:53,045
The seas are full of villains.

274
00:18:53,160 --> 00:18:54,513
What's one more, I say?

275
00:18:56,700 --> 00:18:59,112
Aren't you interested in the new warlord?

276
00:18:59,660 --> 00:19:01,820
I don't give a damn who it is.

277
00:19:02,400 --> 00:19:06,820
Now tell me, did you eliminate the
rat who saw our rainmaking ship?

278
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:08,390
Flawlessly.

279
00:19:13,140 --> 00:19:18,720
They say he's as tall as Whitebeard So
which one of us do you think is stronger,

280
00:19:19,160 --> 00:19:19,990
Koby?

281
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,940
Oh, it's you of course, Lady Ovita?

282
00:19:27,140 --> 00:19:29,957
Gene Bay, they found
a replacement already!

283
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:31,560
Good lucky, huh?

284
00:19:31,860 --> 00:19:33,797
I don't want to hear that from you, Ace.

285
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:34,800
Don't joke!

286
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:37,697
This is your doing.

287
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:41,877
You're the one who beat Hina Buddha and
caused this mess in the first place.

288
00:19:41,960 --> 00:19:45,078
So does the new guy meet
your lofty standards or not?

289
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:47,320
I'm trying to figure that out now.

290
00:19:48,580 --> 00:19:50,000
The man's a former king?

291
00:19:50,240 --> 00:19:51,200
That's a shock.

292
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:54,497
But I suppose he won't be the
only royalty in the group.

293
00:19:54,580 --> 00:19:57,300
The world of pirates
certainly has changed.

294
00:19:58,520 --> 00:20:00,240
This is of no concern to me.

295
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:04,040
I will not be going to
Central no matter what.

296
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:07,065
Such ignorance ill suits
the ruler of our land!

297
00:20:07,820 --> 00:20:08,900
Get back here!

298
00:20:09,280 --> 00:20:10,400
Ah, sissy!

299
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:13,020
It says he has paw pad powers.

300
00:20:13,300 --> 00:20:15,357
Am I supposed to be scared of that?

301
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:18,793
Well, he wouldn't be a warlord
if he was weak, I suppose.

302
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:24,737
But the warlords work directly
under the government, right?

303
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:26,408
That's not the Kuma I know!

304
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:36,000
Dear Bonnie, I'm riding
you for my ship at sea.

305
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:40,173
I've become a bit infamous,
so it's harder to travel now.

306
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:41,638
But I'm doing fine.

307
00:20:44,780 --> 00:20:46,200
Sorry, it's a bit far.

308
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:51,082
How's everyone?

309
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:56,640
I'll try to find all sorts of places that
you and I can visit once you turn ten.

310
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:03,437
Bartholomew Koala, you have a
new order from the government.

311
00:21:03,520 --> 00:21:04,440
Where are you?

312
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:10,280
Oh, it's mad!

313
00:21:11,740 --> 00:21:13,320
I'm in the East Blue.

314
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,060
What is the order?

315
00:21:44,560 --> 00:21:47,360
Let's go.

316
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:23,400
I'll keep smiling.

317
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,337
I'll see you

318
00:22:39,420 --> 00:22:44,120
next time.
